      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "Calculate force frequency from running cadence (steps per minute)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "cadence",
          "label": "Running Cadence",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "steps/min",
          "defaultValue": 150
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "force_frequency",
          "label": "Force Frequency",
          "unit": "Hz",
          "formula": "inputs.cadence / 60",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Activity Frequency Ranges\n\n- **Everyday walking**: 1.0 - 2.0 Hz\n- **Everyday running**: 2.5 Hz (150 steps/min)\n- **Elite running**: 3.3 Hz (200 steps/min)\n- **Dancing**: 1.0 - 3.0 Hz\n\n## Typical Resonance Frequencies\n\n**Wooden Beam Floors**: 5 - 12 Hz (depends on joist span)\n\n**Concrete Floors on Ground**: 10 - 100 Hz (depends on soil type)\n\n### Ground Material Impact\n- Sand: 15 - 25 Hz\n- Clay (wet): 15 Hz\n- Clay (hard): 30 Hz\n- Gravel: 20 - 25 Hz\n- Limestone: 35 - 45 Hz\n- Solid rock: 40 - 50 Hz"
    }
  ]
